   "resumo_en": "Wisconsin Death Trip is the debut studio album by American industrial metal band Static-X, released on March 23, 1999, by Warner Bros. Records. \nThe band was formed after lead singer Wayne Static and drummer Ken Jay met at a Virgin Records store in Chicago, and later relocated to California. Tony Campos joined on bass, followed soon after by guitarist Koichi Fukuda. Warner Brothers Records signed them in February 1998.\nWisconsin Death Trip peaked at number 107 on the US Billboard 200 and number one on the Top Heatseekers chart, and was certified platinum by the RIAA in 2001. Four singles were released from the album: \"Push It\", \"I'm with Stupid\", \"Bled for Days\" and \"Love Dump\".",
