   "resumo_en": "Machine is the second studio album by American industrial metal band Static-X, released on May 22, 2001, and recorded at Studio 508 (Los Angeles). When compared to the band's other albums, Machine features more electronics and industrial effects, and more screamed vocals from Wayne Static. It was also the final studio album to feature all four original Static-X members, until 2020's Project: Regeneration Vol. 1 (which featured archival content left behind by Static after his death in 2014).",
