   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cult_of_Static",
   "resumo_en": "Cult of Static is the sixth studio album by American industrial metal band Static-X. It was released on March 17, 2009 via Reprise Records. The album's first single \"Stingwray\" was released and made available on the band's MySpace page on February 17, 2009. The album's title is a reference to the die-hard fans who have supported the band for so long. This would be Static-X's last studio album for eleven years, as well as the last to feature drummer Nick Oshiro and founding member and vocalist Wayne Static during his lifetime, though the latter's posthumously released work was included on the band's Project Regeneration albums. Cult of Static also marked the last time Static-X worked with John Travis, and was the band's last album on Reprise Records.",
